<title>USA: Harley-Davidson rises on strong Q1.</title>
<headline>Harley-Davidson rises on strong Q1.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Harley-Davidson Inc roared ahead 3-1/8 to 38 Tuesday on the horsepower provided by better-than-expected first quarter financial results.</p>
<p>The Milwaukee motorcycle builder reported late Monday that it earned $0.53 per share in the three months ended March 30, compared with $0.44 per share in the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>Wall Street analysts said they had expected Harley to report quarterly profits closer to $0.48-$0.49 per share.</p>
<p>&quot;It was well above what the Street was looking for,&quot; said S&amp;P Equity Group industry analyst Michael Pizzi.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
